{
  "tema": 6237,
  "slug": "sustantivos-ista-crata",
  "titulo": "Gender of nouns and adjectives ending in -ista and -crata",
  "subtitulo": "El dentista / la dentista: the article tells you who.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "Nouns ending in -ista and -crata have the same form for both genders; only the article changes: el / la dentista, los / las demócratas.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Nouns ending in **-ista** and **-crata** usually refer to people, and they have **one form** for men and women. Only the **article** changes."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "",
            "Masculine",
            "Feminine"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "singular",
              "el dentista",
              "la dentista"
            ],
            [
              "plural",
              "los dentistas",
              "las dentistas"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The plural just adds **-s**. A mixed group takes **los**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Many are jobs or people who support an idea: **periodista**, **futbolista**, **artista**, **taxista**, **electricista**, **ciclista**, **feminista**; **demócrata**, **burócrata**, **aristócrata**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "As adjectives they also have one form: **un chavo optimista**, **una chava optimista**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **-ista** never changes its clothes; the article does the talking."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==El dentista== me puso una resina ayer.",
              "en": "The dentist gave me a filling yesterday."
            },
            {
              "es": "==La dentista== dice que me lave los dientes diario.",
              "en": "The dentist (female) says to brush my teeth every day."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Los dentistas== se reunieron en el colegio médico.",
              "en": "The dentists met at the medical association."
            },
            {
              "es": "Naomi es ==mecánica== y ==una gran artista==.",
              "en": "Naomi is a mechanic and a great artist."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermana es ==periodista==.",
              "en": "My sister is a journalist."
            },
            {
              "es": "==El taxista== nos dejó en la playa.",
              "en": "The taxi driver dropped us at the beach."
            },
            {
              "es": "Es ==una persona muy optimista==.",
